{
 "what": "drive-vs-decay mu criterion (arXiv 2610.02344v1) vs our race N1 (rank_pred) on delivered runs",
 "definition": "Baseline: the drive-vs-decay stability-ratio criterion of De Melo Costa et al. (arXiv 2610.02344v1,\nsubmitted 2026-10-01; code github.com/jose-melo/drive-vs-decay @ 3176215, 2026-10-01), scored on the\ndelivered held-out linear runs (E1b) and masking runs (E2) against the same measured ranks as our race (N1).\n\nTheir criterion (paper Sec. 3.2-3.3, Eq. 4-8, Table 3):\n  linearise W at W = Wa = 0 with the predictor Wp held at its initial value (their Lemma 3.4);\n  drive gamma = c_k q_l, decay sigma = a_k p_l, where a_k, c_k are eigen/singular values of Sigma_11, Sigma_X1\n  along data mode k and p_l, q_l eigenvalues of Wp^T Wp, Wp^T M2 (singular-value form: p_l = s_l^2,\n  q_l = s_l with s_l the singular values of Wp; no feature-side target mask here, M2 = I);\n  pairing of a_k and c_k: eigenvector-paired absolute form (their Eq. 51, used for their main-text r_tight);\n  Eq. (31) (independently sorted singular values) and the signed paired form (App. C.8) as variants;\n  weight decay enters as an additive floor (Table 3): a pair (k, l) is unstable iff c_k q_l > a_k p_l + lam;\n  the EMA rate does not move the boundary (constant term of their characteristic equation);\n  predicted rank = r_tight = min(|pi_l U|, |pi_k U|, d, N) with U the unstable pairs (Cor. 3.3).\n  'dvd_nowd' is the same count without the weight-decay floor (the mu > 1 boundary of their Eq. 6).\nPredictor side (review experiment-repo#11): 'dvd', 'dvd_signed', 'dvd_sorted' take q_l = s_l, the singular value of\n  Wp (the Eq. 31 proxy, also what their code 3176215 _compute_multimode_mu uses). Eq. 7/51 define q_l along\n  predictor mode l; paired on the eigenvectors v_l of Wp^T Wp that is q_l = v_l^T Wp^T v_l, |q_l| <= s_l:\n  'dvd_pq' (Eq. 51 paired, absolute c_k and q_l) and 'dvd_pq_signed' (Eq. 7 paired, signed c_k and q_l).\n  'dvd_exact' is the same linearisation without their decoupling (the route of their App. A.5):\n  dW/dt = -Wp^T Wp W S11 + Wp^T W S21 - lam W, i.e. J = S21^T (x) Wp^T - S11 (x) Wp^T Wp - lam I; U = the\n  invariant subspace of eigenvalues with Re > 0; |pi_k U| = dimension of the data-side (row) span of its\n  eigenvectors as matrices, |pi_l U| = dimension of their column span, predicted rank min(|pi_k U|, |pi_l U|, d).\n  All variants coincide when Wp is a multiple of the identity and the data spectra are aligned.\n  'ass32' marks runs inside their Assumption 3.2 (Sigma_11, Sigma_X1, Wp^T Wp and Wp share an eigenbasis);\n  E1b randpred and noncomm, E2 block_nc and MLP-feature statistics fall outside it.\nTheir r_tight is an upper bound, not a prediction of ERank (their Prop. C.4), so each score also reports\n'exceed', the share of runs whose measured rank is above the predicted count; near collapse their Cor. 3.3 with\nLemma 3.4 says it should be near 0.\nIn the aligned arms (identity predictor, total gain p0) the criterion coincides with the delivered\n'static initial window' #{p0 c_k - p0^2 s_k - lam > 0}; this script recomputes it from their definition.\nArms outside their framework are skipped: no stop-gradient (nosg), fixed P = I (nopred, E1b), Adam;\nfinite-batch arms (E1b batch, E2 sgd) are scored with population statistics, as for N1.\nUsage: python3 code/baselines/dvd_mu.py results/baselines\nInputs: results/e1b/e1b_runs.csv, results/e2/e2_runs.csv (measured ranks), code/e1b.py, code/e2.py (statistics, inits).\n",
 "keys": {
  "rank_pred": "delivered race prediction (N1 / N1-general), as pre-registered",
  "dvd": "their r_tight (Eq. 51-52, eigenvector-paired absolute form, the main-text metric) with the weight-decay floor of Table 3",
  "dvd_nowd": "the same without weight decay (mu > 1)",
  "dvd_signed": "their signed form (App. C.8): paired, c_k with sign, with weight decay",
  "dvd_sorted": "their Eq. (31) form: data spectra sorted independently, with weight decay",
  "dvd_pq": "Eq. 51 paired on both sides: |c_k| on eigenvectors of Sigma_11, |q_l| = |v_l^T Wp^T v_l| on eigenvectors of Wp^T Wp, with weight decay",
  "dvd_pq_signed": "Eq. 7 paired, signed c_k and q_l, with weight decay",
  "dvd_exact": "exact linearisation at W = 0 with Wp fixed, no decoupling (their App. A.5 route), with weight decay",
  "ass32": "1 if the run satisfies their Assumption 3.2 (shared eigenbasis of Sigma_11, Sigma_X1, Wp, Wp^T Wp)",
  "rank_window": "delivered static initial window (as delivered)",
  "rank_bound": "static threshold c^2 >= 4 lam s"
 },
